.Dd October 10, 2026
.Dt NETWORKCMPCTL 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm networkcmpctl
.Nd inspect the network broker and sampled interface state
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm config
.Nm
.Cm info
.Nm
.Cm state-watch
.Op Ar count Op Ar timeout-ms
.Nm
.Cm listen
.Nm
.Cm connect
.Ar addr Ar port
.Nm
.Cm udp
.Ar addr Ar port
.Nm
.Cm resolve
.Op Fl 4 | Fl 6
.Op Fl m
.Op Fl a
.Ar host
.Op Ar service
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a bounded diagnostic client for a NetworkCmp session injected by
.Xr switchboard 8 .
All live operations reach the broker through
.Xr libnetworkcmp 3
and receive no additional network authority; the
.Cm listen
self-test additionally opens one ordinary loopback socket to drive the
listener it was handed.
.Pp
.Nm
is approved software.
Its exec manifest declares the
.Dq system.network.admin
software attribute, so the kernel-attributed image opens the broker through
.Dq system.Network.Admin ,
which requires that attribute, including from a login session that cannot
resolve
.Dq system.Network .
Copying or replacing the binary does not carry the attribute.
.Pp
The commands are:
.Bl -tag -width resolve
.It Cm config
Print the canonical service-manifest declaration for this local component.
.It Cm info
Print the feature mask, and resolver result
bound.
.It Cm listen
Exercise the listening-endpoint capability end to end: obtain a listening
descriptor on an OS-assigned loopback port from the broker, connect to it,
accept the connection, and verify a byte flows.
Requires the label's
.Cm listen
policy.
.It Cm connect Ar addr Ar port
Exercise the connect capability: ask the broker to open a connected TCP
socket to the numeric
.Ar addr
and
.Ar port
(bounded by a short timeout).
Subject to the label's connect policy and the internal-destination (SSRF)
filter.
.It Cm udp Ar addr Ar port
Exercise the datagram capability: ask the broker to open a connected
.Dv SOCK_DGRAM
socket to the numeric
.Ar addr
and
.Ar port .
Proves the born-in-capmode broker reaches the UDP connect path (a connected
descriptor, or an ordinary network error, never
.Er ECAPMODE ) .
Subject to the label's connect policy and the internal-destination filter.
.It Cm resolve Ar host Op Ar service
Resolve a name through the component's bounded resolver and print each typed
endpoint.
The optional
.Fl 4
and
.Fl 6
select IPv4 and IPv6 respectively; the default requests both.
With
.Fl 6 ,
.Fl m
allows IPv4-mapped IPv6 results when native IPv6 results are absent, and
.Fl a
requests both native and mapped results.
.Fl a
requires
.Fl m .
Use
.Fl -
to end option parsing before the hostname.
These flags also apply to numeric addresses and the local hosts snapshot.
Temporary DNS failures are reported as errors and are not retried by this tool.
The printed TTL is the remaining conservative DNS lifetime; zero advertises
no positive cache lifetime, including numeric and local hosts results.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Pa /Capabilities/System/NetworkControl.cap/Units/networkcmpctl.unit/Unit.ucl
exec manifest approving
.Nm
with
.Dq system.network.admin
and
.Dq system.network.observe .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Pa /Capabilities/System/NetworkControl.cap/Units/networkcmpctl.unit/Unit.ucl
exec manifest approving
.Nm
with
.Dq system.network.admin .
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh STATE OBSERVATION
.Cm state-watch Op Ar count Op Ar timeout-ms
prints interface state snapshots, defaulting to one snapshot and an infinite
watch timeout.
Count must be from 1 through 4294967295.
Timeout is a nonnegative millisecond value; 4294967295 means infinite and
zero polls for an immediately available change.
Each snapshot includes epoch, generation, source_error, and count,
followed by escaped interface names, flags, MTU, and link state.
Output is flushed after every snapshot for use in pipes.
A nonzero source_error means unavailable data, not an empty inventory.
A watch timeout exits unsuccessfully.
.Pp
This command uses
.Va system.Network.State
through the tool's approved
.Va system.network.observe
attribute.
It reports sampled state, not every interface transition or Internet
connectivity.
See
.Xr network_state 3 .
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr libnetworkcmp 3 ,
.Xr switchboard 5 ,
.Xr BSDNetwork 8 ,
.Xr switchboard 8
